# The build context is the repository root. Everything is excluded, and only
# what the Dockerfile reads is admitted again: go.mod, go.sum, the source
# trees the supervisor is compiled from, and the two example files copied
# into the image. A directory added to the repository later stays outside the
# context until a rule below names it, so local tooling, working notes and
# build output cannot reach the published image by being forgotten. A file
# dropped inside one of the trees admitted below is a different matter: the
# first stage copies the whole context and would carry it in a layer of its
# own. The final stage copies the compiled binary out of that stage and the
# two example files by name, and the build exports no cache, so nothing else
# the first stage holds is published.
*

!go.mod
!go.sum
!adapter
!cmd
!examples/pipeline

# Not read by the build, even inside the trees admitted above. These patterns
# are unanchored, so they also catch a node_modules or a coverage profile
# left inside the example by a local command.
**/node_modules
**/bin
**/docs
**/testdata
**/*_test.go
**/*.out
**/*.test
**/*.prof
**/*.exe

# Files beside the example that describe or build it rather than being read
# by the image.
examples/pipeline/Dockerfile
examples/pipeline/README.md
examples/pipeline/graph.yaml
